\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Left: the radial acceleration relation for 164 SPARC galaxies (3284 points, $Q \leq 2$). The red curve is the GFD field equation, equation~(\ref {eq:prediction}), with $a_0 = 1.2 \times 10^{-10}$~m/s$^2$; the orange dotted curve is the McGaugh et al.\ (2016) empirical fit. The dashed line is the Newtonian expectation $g_{\rm  obs} = g_{\rm  bar}$. Right: residual histograms ($\log g_{\rm  obs} - \log g_{\rm  theory}$) for both curves. The two distributions are nearly identical.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rar}{{1}{3}{Left: the radial acceleration relation for 164 SPARC galaxies (3284 points, $Q \leq 2$). The red curve is the GFD field equation, equation~(\ref {eq:prediction}), with $a_0 = 1.2 \times 10^{-10}$~m/s$^2$; the orange dotted curve is the McGaugh et al.\ (2016) empirical fit. The dashed line is the Newtonian expectation $g_{\rm obs} = g_{\rm bar}$. Right: residual histograms ($\log g_{\rm obs} - \log g_{\rm theory}$) for both curves. The two distributions are nearly identical}{figure.1}{}}
